<http://home.us.net/~satterle/mcse/nt-arch/nt-arch.html> has a good
diagram of the NT architecture. Notice that the device drivers and
windows managers bypass the HAL and kernel and go directly to the
hardware. This means 3 things. First games can run real fast. Second
GUIs can trash everything. Thirdly, there are some security exploits
that are not fixable. Thankfully most of those exploits are beyond the
abilities of script kiddies. Most people who can exploit them won't.
Those who can and will are really dangerous.


