>
[snip]
> I heard a story some time ago that at about NT 4 the whole layered
> access system (like VMS's user-supervisor-exec-kernel) was broken so
> that software for games could directly access hardware devices and hence
> make the games run faster.  If that is someone's idea of security and
> reliability ....
>
> Can anyone shed any more light on this ?
>

This is a red herring (and you have the story slightly wrong).  In NT V4,
the graphics subsystem was moved into the kernel.  Prior to that it ran as a
separate process.  So in V4 it's running in kernel mode and prior to that it
was running in user mode.  Some people like to throw this up as a change
that made NT less reliable because if the graphics subsystem has a problem,
it crashes the whole system since it's now running in kernel mode.  In
reality, it had very little affect on the reliability of NT because in V3.x,
if the graphics subsystem died the kernel would notice and force a system
crash.





