OK, you can force a UNIX system to emulate some aspects of the VMS way of
handling symbolic names. It's not general, every application that needs
to operate that way has to be specifically coded to implement it, but if
you wantto insist on using a procedural programming model with global
variables instead of the "pure function" dataflow model UNIX uses you can
get that kind of behaviour.

You can get the effect of a goto in Lisp, if you want. You just have to
write your program as a big cond inside a loop and change the state variable
the cond uses. You can write procedural code in Prolog. You can write
dataflow code in VMS... I even implemented a shell in RSX-11 about 18
years ago, back before I realised that it was better to use the system the
way it's designed rather than trying to make it look like UNIX (or VMS:
I use DCL on VMS, MCR on RSX).

> To
>be of general use, all shell forms need to be supported so the
