> may terminate the command running, not the DCL .COM.

This is the documented behavior. SET CONTROL is subject to the current
state of error traping. SET NOON (NO ON) over-rides SET CONTROL in that
CTRL+Y may terminate a command (especially if its external), but the
procedure which invoked the command will ignore the $STATUS returned if
SET NOON is in force.

