 My system is a 164LX, so my experience may not apply, but I can tell
you that not all ECC registered RAM is equal. I've heard/read
conflicting reasons, but it is a fact that not just any ECC registered
DIMMs will work properly on the LX. I got mine with 2 64M DIMMs
installed, so I knew the board & CPU worked. I also am blessed with a
supplier who lets me try memory before I buy it, on non-PC hardware. We
went through 18 pieces, 9 different pairs of different brands & sizes,
of DIMMs that *exactly* match DEC's specs for the LX board. Some pairs
would POST, up to the memory tests, and hang, some would go through the
whole post, but not boot the OS. I finally gave up and paid the price
for Kingston RAM specifically for the LX, and it works flawlessly.
 You might also try attaching a serial terminal on the first port. You
may have "console" set to "serial", which turns off VGA. If you don't
have a terminal, a null-modem cable to a PC and minicom or Hyperterm
will work.

	Doc


