No one is more aware of Perl's faults than those responsible for its
care and feeding (which in a very minor role includes me).  However,
for those more interested in getting work done than in making
doctrinaire dismissals, it's quite handy to have in the toolbox.  As
far as loose quotes sneaking in, it has much more aggressive
diagnostics than DCL.

