Some of the most important parts of your windoz systems are not part of 
MS Windows.  Many device drivers are provided by the manufacturer of the 
device.  They do this in order to sell their devices to all those windoz 
users out there.  They do not provide drivers for any other OS, that I 
know of.

Not sure how this is handled for Linux and the other unicies.

VMS on IA-32 isn't the major issue.  Drivers for devices on IA-32 
systems running VMS is the biggest issue.  Having such devices actually 
match their declared specifications is another major issue.  Windoz may 
not use all options in a specification, and therefore get away with 
using the device.  VMS will use any and all stated capabilities in the 
interest of performance.  Many devices that are used on windoz systems 
will die on a VMS system.

