What do the eight LED's on the back of the machine say in hex?  It
sounds like the console is set to serial, so you'll need to hook up a
terminal or terminal emulator to COM1 (9600 8bit No Parity).  Use a
DecConnect cable to an H8571-J adapter if you have a Dec terminal.

LED E2 means floppy load failed
LED E5 means console initialized and you should have >>> or auto_action
was initiated.

Little known item - LED on floppy drive is turned on by the controller,
even if there is no power to floppy drive, so check the little floppy
power connector.  There is a jumper to enable the flash (j4), but the
default is flash enabled, I do believe.

Also, if the FSL finally loads the firmware correctly, I don't know if
it will retain the console setting or default to one or the other.  In
any case, if it ends up set to serial, you won't be changing it to
graphics without going to a serial connection first.

A keyboard error might possibly change the console from graphics to
serial, but that is a little hazy.

Check everything above, and you should be on your way.  Actually, there
may be nothing wrong with it except the console setting.  Good luck!




