When the Alphastation passes all of the self-tests, it will stop and
display ">>>", assuming the "os_type" isn't set to NT.  (The ">>>" is
commonly called the "triple-arrow prompt".)

The "E5" in the LED's you described says the console is initialized and
is waiting at the triple arrow prompt.  You just can't see it, most
likely because the console is set for serial output to a terminal via
serial port 1.  So, it will be necessary to hook up a terminal or
terminal emulator to serial port 1 in order to get the machine working.

When you get to the triple arrow prompt via serial port 1, type the
following:
>>> set console graphics <return>
>>>

After that, rebooting will output console data to both serial port 1 and
the monitor.


