Your friend can save time as SYSTEM by just typing SHUTDOWN.
It has been a default abbreviation in SYS$MANAGER:LOGIN.COM for years.

> UNIX entered the 100% secure mode (I.E. the machine was powered off) in
> about 2 minutes.  VMS, however, took around 5 minutes to get to the point
> where we could turn the VAX off.
> 
> See?  Proof, I can secure UNIX more then twice as fast as OpenVMS!

If you cut the power to your VMS machine it will be equally secure.
The careful-write approach taken by RMS ensures disk integrity.
Any fixup you choose to perform as part of reboot just recovers
unused disk blocks to the pool -- the file system is intact without
it.


