Once you have cache, though, this doesn't save you anything and has the
disadvantage of making it very difficult to pipeline accesses to the
accumulators, and someone else has already mentioned what this does to
separate I&D caching.

Not that the vax is particularly easy to pipeline. You need just-in-time
translation techniques to make the VAX run really fast. And they became
really practical far too late for the VAX, though I understand DEC came
up with a nice software JIT engine for the VAX-Alpha transition.

