For example, a very simple piece of C code that shows a buffer exploit without
having to actually run code on the stack:

void hole(char *url) {
	char tempurl[512];
	char flags;	/* 1=admin, 2=guest, 4=wheel */
	char *p,*p2;
	int i=0;

	p=tempurl; p2=url;
	while (*p2) *p++=*p2++;

	{lots of other code that uses the flags to do things with}
}

Then, call hole with 513 char URL with the last character being ASCII
code for "1". This will fill flags with (octal) 61 and the admin flag
will be set.

