That would surprise me a bit, since when I left after V3 (IIRC) shipped the
EOL handwriting appeared to be on the wall.

That was the release that supported Ethernet LAN with workstations (which
could be diskless) transparently sharing one or more server systems.
Suddenly the servers required environments supporting multiple users, and we
implemented that by adding a directory level to isolate them from each other
(plus I think mapping hacks to make each user's domain appear to be an MFD
so that all the existing software would continue to run without change).
