These are not "standard" power supplies, as I am sure you know.

IIRC, the original power supply for the AS250 4/266 became 
unavailable 2 or more years ago, and the PSU from the AS200 4/233 
was sold instead as a replacement for the one the AS250 shipped 
with.  They have a smaller max output power (180W), and don't 
have a power connector in the back for you to plug in your monitor 
or other sundry peripherals.  Cost from Compaq was $106.  

I recently tried to procure one of these from Compaq and from a 
couple of the DEC resellers.  I had done this a couple times in 
the past. I tried Compaq first - they told me that the part is 
no longer available.  The other places I tried (NE Digital and 
somewhere else - can't recall) could not get one for me, either.

[Historically, this worked out great for me, as I saved a couple 
 of AS250s with bad PSUs from my old job that were destined for 
 the scrap heap; got them working again for just over 100 bucks 
 each.]

Anyway, the part number for the replacement PSU (i.e., the 
180W one) is

30-44170-01

It is still listed on 

http://www.compaq.com/CAS-Catalog/das046hm.html

for the same price of $106.  Good luck getting one, though.  
I hope you can.

Failing the above, you could hang around Ebay looking for a 
bargain AS200 4/233.  That's what I did when I ran into this 
problem a few months ago.  I got one for $100 or so.

