All rumours are that the reason for the gross delays in the EV6 and
EV7 were quite simply because of lack of resources.  And, comparing
the EV7 with the EV6, the situation was getting worse over time.
Note that by "the EVx" I am also referring to chipsets and so on,
without which the chip is useless and cannot support faster clock
speeds even on the same chip - witness the 1 GHz Alpha and ES45
shambles.

Furthermore, there is more to this sort of thing than just the
hardware.  The operating systems need work (and major work) if the
parallelism is to be much increased.  The compilers need major work
if the memory management has been radically changed and so on.

Now, the POWER4 is released with interim compilers and operating
systems (which probably work but have not been optimised for it),
but we have a schedule for their delivery.  When are the comparable
software upgrades for the EV7 due?  Does ANYONE know, even Capellas?


