My measurements were extremely subjective.  If I had to fight
with OS everytime I wanted to do something and then, when I
had finally convinced it to do the task, the elapsed time 
caused me to fidget, I considered the OS distasteful.  My
IAS experience was certifying DECnet.  I didn't have problems
booting the system, running the scripts.  <gasp> I could even
go away and let it run with confidence that the damn thing
would not barf due to loneliness (this was prevalent with RSTS).
I didn't get into the internals of IAS to see what they were
doing well.  Perhaps I should but I simply didn't have the time.


