Describe the VMS implementation of: COMND, recognition/completion,
GTJFN/GNJFN/JFNS, TTLNK, ? (or /? if you want to be Microsoftish), and
PMAP (be sure to detail all forms).

Explain DCL; a command language so ridiculous that it makes UNIX look like
a marvel of good design by comparison.  Why, for example, is an
infrequently used function such as the one to attach to another process
honored with a top-level verb command, whereas the commonly used function
to change the working directory a subverb of SET (and why such an obscure
one as that -- doesn't VMS have any other defaults)?

Describe the VMS commands to analyze why a program which just crashed did
so, and how the crashed process can be restarted with the problem
remedied.  Oh, and no running it under a debugger beforehand; it's got to
be completely post-mortem.

