Check out lib$file* and lib$find_file, lib$file_fid_to_name.etc. and
associated underlying services for approx equivalents to gtjfn,gnjfn
and jfns. No direct TTLNK call but apps which hook into the tty
drivers and provide that functionality are available. As to PMAP with
"detail all forms" I think I'd want to spend some time with both the
TOPS-20 Monitor calls manual and VMS docs before taking a stab at that
one. Too many options. You can certainly map a file section to disk in
VMS though.

>
>Explain DCL; a command language so ridiculous that it makes UNIX look like
