DEBUG/RESUME (the default)

Notice in the example below the program was specifically run /NODEBUG
and then later the debugger started as you specified. You do not have
to link/debug either unless you want high level language (source code)
stepping.

From HELP DEBUG

  2.$ FORTRAN/DEBUG/NOOPTIMIZE WIDGET
         $ LINK/DEBUG WIDGET
         $ RUN/NODEBUG WIDGET

           NAME:
           NAME:
           NAME:
         ^Y
         $ DEBUG/RESUME

                      [ Debugger Banner and Version ]

           %DEBUG-I-INITIAL, language is FORTRAN, module set to WIDGET
           DBG>

         The FORTRAN and LINK commands both specify the /DEBUG
qualifier
         to compile the program WIDGET.FOR with debugger symbol table


Press RETURN to continue ...

         information. The RUN command begins execution of the image
