have always been there.  (example: -lm to get the math library for C).

Somehow VMS reminds me of what my high school geometry teacher
used to say about our proofs: "Why do it the easy way when there 
is a hard way?"   Unix tries to be simple in design, maybe not
simple to use.  VMS tries to be complicated even if simple would work.

I still remember trying to figure out the DCL command interpreter,
and the way to add new commands by compiling a special command
description language.  Compare that to unix shell filename expansion,
and argc/argv for command processing.  

-- glen


