> what do the run levels of DU 0-9 equate to?  
> WHich is the right level for multiuser mode?
> where are the docs that cover this? Ain't in the man pages from what I 
> can find.
> thanks
> bob

Dear Bob,

	default multiuser runlevel is 3. Have a look at /etc/inittab.
It will give you some ideas. 'man inittab' helps further.
The run levels are as follows:
 0         Specifies the halt state.
 2         Specifies multiuser state without network services.
 3         Specifies multiuser state with network services.
 S or s    Specifies single-user state.
 
