Problem has been resolved.  I would recommend removing the firmware update
file from the cdrom and making a boot disk to manually update the firmware.
My confidence in Compaq has just dropped another notch because apparently it
is a fault in the cd.

Solution: (For those who are curious)

copy the mkbootfirm and fwupdate.exe from cdrom provided by compaq or
download from ftp.digital.com
insert blank floppy into a working Tru64 Unix Box
fddisk -fmt /dev/disk/floppy0c (Formats the floppy)
cd (to the directory where files were downloaded to)
chmod +x ./mkbootfirm (make this executable)
./mkbootfirm fwupdate.exe | dd of=/dev/floppy0c bs=64k (makes it a bootable
floppy)

Once this was done I went to the now non-working box removed the cover and
set the jumper so it would boot from disk.  Refer to your Owners manual for
this one.

Turned power on and it booted from the floppy.
I then told it to update the firmware once again and everything went
fine......
Turned power off....reset jumper and rebooted.
Everything is now working great.

I'm sure there's other ways around this too but this is what worked for
me......



