sword7@speakeasy.org wrote:
> 
> Hello folks:
> 
> Help! I struggled to install NetBSD/vax into SIMH emulator.  I tried
> to enter /dev/ra1a as RRD40 but I was told that they are not found
> (vax/binary/sets directory).
> 
> Does anyone know about NetBSD/vax installation?  Has anyone successfully
> installed NetBSD/vax on Simh emulator?

I managed to get it to work.  The steps below are from memory, and
may be out of sequence.

After getting into the install, it asks for where it is to load from
(choose cdrom), then asks for the device/directory to install from.
Change the device from 'ca0'(?) to 'ra0' or which ever unit the cd is
mounted on.

It should then ask for the destination drive 'ra1' (or whatever unit
the blank RD is mounted on).

It will then ask for type of install (standard, X, custom),
which just determines the partition table. Pick standard, X will
never fit and you don't have network devices or graphic display
anyway. It should then format the drive.

It will then ask for what to install, choose custom.  Turn off all of
the X stuff, the games, and the manuals (RD54 is just too small).
It asks if you want to display file names as they are installed.
Pick 'yes' so you don't think it has died.

It will set with 'netbsd' listed for a minute or so, then will
start to list files.  You then go into date/time settings, and
root password.  It should finally exit to shell, then shut down.

Reboot onto the RD, and play.



