>    doing record management and came up with a common RMS).

Seth Cohen wrote RMS-20 concurrently with our writing RMS-11 (and it may
have predated RMS-32 on VAX by a bit).  RMS-11 was just as much of a
retrofit (i.e., just as un-'predefined', and for that matter also was
process-level code) on RSX and RSTS as RMS-20 was, and even VMS didn't have
its own full-blown RMS in V1 (indexed file support was available only by
running RMS-11 in emulation).

