As far as device ID's, we have 5 for the TU81, 9 for TQK50 and the oldest
TUK50's, 14 for the TQK70, 25 for the later TUK50's, 65 for a TK50
on a DEBNT, 98 for a TF85, 99 for a TF70, 103 for the TF837 and
TF70L, and 110 for TF86.

> because I want to
>develop TMSCP emulation for my TS10/VAX emulator. Does anyone have
>a listing of tape geometries with media id and device type?

Where the "disk geometry" bytes reside in a MSCP message there
are various "tape" items that you might think of as geometries.

In particular at the octal offsets shown below we have:

P.SHUN= 40      ;  2 Shadow unit (disk)  density (tape)
P.SHST= 42      ;  2 Shadow status (disk)   speed (ips*bpi/1000) (tape)
P.TRCK= 44      ;  2 Track size (disk)  format menu (tape)
P.GRP=  46      ;  2 Group size (disk)  max write byte count (tape)
P.CYL=  50      ;  2 Cylinder size (disk)   max noise rec size (tape)

where the masks for density are

DENTBL: TBLENT  1       ,<NRZI 800 BPI>
        TBLENT  2       ,<PE 1600 BPI>
        TBLENT  4       ,<GCR 6250 BPI>
        TBLENT  10      ,<Cartridge (TK50)>
        TBLENT  401     ,<NRZI 800 BPI>
        TBLENT  402     ,<PE 1600 BPI>
        TBLENT  404     ,<GCR 6250 BPI>
        TBLENT  420     ,<TU82 special high density>;according to RSTS/E
        TBLENT  1001    ,<Cartridge (TK50)>
        TBLENT  1002    ,<Cartridge (TK70)>
        ;       20xx entries are supposed to be RV80, whatever that is,

At one point I knew why there were two different entries for 800, 1600,
and 6250 BPI, but I don't remember anymore.

Tim.



