Bruce Lane wrote:

>         This is great news. I wondered if there was any common sense left
> at HP after their ridiculous spin-off of their test gear branch.

The only thing ridiculous about the Agilent spinoff was that the wrong
company
got to keep the HP name.  HP originally moved into computers to provide
"smarts"
for their test gear. It grew into a big business, especially the printer
part of
it.  And it just didn't make sense after a while for this huge PC
company to also make
test equipment.  Ok, if they were GE they might have been able to pull
that off, but
HP is not GE. Besides, from the test equipment side PCs are commodity
parts, like
screws or lightbulbs.  Since the split Agilent has presumably been free
to ship
Dell PCs with their test equipment - just like the vast majority of
other test
equipment suppliers.  If they've taken advantage of that opportunity
they're likely
now able to ship the same configuration for less than they would have
were they
still required to use HP PCs.

Regards,

David Mathog
