> >
> >Directory DU0:[2,54]
> >29-JAN-88 12:29
> >
> >MUDRV.TSK;1         12.     C  04-SEP-85 13:48
> >MUDRV.STB;1         2.         04-SEP-85 13:48
> >
> >Total of 14./14. blocks in 2. files
> >
> >>LOAD MU:
> >LOA -- Open failure on file MUDRV.STB
> >

[2,54] holds the baseline system that is distributed on the original kit.
This
system can be booted on just about all configurations and it enables the
user
to do a sysgen for their own particular config. This has been done on your
system but whoever did it didn't include the MU driver.

So, try:

>BOO [2,54]RSX11M

when the baseline system boots:

>LOA MU:
>CON ONL ALL

and that should get the TK50 working.

Regards,
Chris.




