You have run into a generic problem with Adobe Acrobat, not specific to the
1152.  With the small amount of memory in the 1152, it is still possible that
one of the following will work:

1. When printing with Acrobat, select the Print as Image checkbox.  This forces
Acrobat to format a bitmap image of the page to be printed.
2. Install the Hewlett-Packard LaserJet IIIp printer driver for the 1152.  This
is a close match for the PCL4 built into the printer.
3. You can also reduce the resolution to 150 dpi, but the printed pages would be
UGLY.

Most of all, see if you can get more memory for the printer.  The max is either
4MB or 5MB, I forget which... Ben Myers

