Robert DiRosario <rdirosario@starpower.net> writes:
> I can't get my RA81 drive working.

  It's been a very long time, but I'll try to help...

> I have a 4000/106A with a B400x.    I've tried three different KDA50
> board sets.   (I don't know if they work.)  When I push in the A and B
> switches they do not light up.   I tried A, B, and "A and B", same
> result.  Both lamps remain off.  "Show device" on the computer lists the
> controller but it doesn't see the drive.  I also tried connecting only
> the A port, but it still doesn't work.  (From my SOC's it looks like you
> can connect both ports to the same controller if you want.)
>
> What causes the A and B port lights to go on?  A simple "DC" path to the
> controller?  A "high level" link?  (I don't know anything about
> SDI disks.)

  The lights go on when the controller establishes a path to the drive
via the MSCP "online" command issued by the driver.

  The most likely problem is an incorrect number of SDI cables. It isn't
immediately obvious at first, but the SDI cable bulkhead flips the pins.
Thus, you need an even number of bulkheads (normally 2, one for the drive
cabinet and one for the CPU cabinet) and an odd number of cables (the
integrated cable between the drive and the drive cabinet bulkhead, the
integrated cable from the controller to the CPU cabinet bulkhead, and
a generic SDI cable (BC26V, I think) between the two bulkheads. If you
try to rig something up by plugging both the drive and Controller cables
into a single bulkhead, you have the wrong number of flips.

