  Yup. These come in both 3-high and 4-high cabinets.

> Does VMS support dual port access to RA drives or does it only use port and
> switch to the other one if the first port/path fails?

  I'm pretty sure a drive can be online on only a single path. The design
for large systems was one or more hosts (VAXex, DECsystems) connected via
dual CI paths to a Star Coupler (which was one box w/ two independent CI
hubs) and then a number of HSC controllers connected to the Star COuplers.
The RA-series disks and TA-series tapes would have a path to each of the
two HSC's. The HSC was a full MSCP server and could serve blocks to all of
the host systems, which would use the distributed lock manager to make
sure they all had a consistent view of the disk data.

  There may be restrictions on cabling the same drive to the same host via
multiple paths (2 cables to the same controller, or a cable to each of two
controllers). I remember situations where the drive would "ping-pong" be-
tween its ports in this case (and there is a rather long timeout on port
selection - 25 seconds IIRC - so this was a pain).

  Older Massbus drives could be accessed on both ports, though DEC oper-
ating systems enforced read-only access in this case.

