Greetings from Antonio,

I hope I am not coming across as rude, but you guys seem to attach to all
things DEC like a baby to its mother. I'm not here to argue the merits or
lack thereof of Dec, but really?

Reading the posts in this newsgroup is like getting trapped in a time warp.
I can't beleive you guys are still talking Dec!

You people need to stop clinging to old technology like its the only thing
you know. The whole world has passed you by.

I cut my teeth on Dec stuff, been around it for years - it used to be my
bread and butter. But I moved on, I adapted to new technology and went with
the flow - for better or worse. I left the past in the past. No good looking
back you know....

Face the facts - Dec is dead and has been for a long time now, but you guys
just can't seem to let go.

I remember the days when transistors started to replace the vacuum tube, and
you guessed it, there were people that beleived it was all things evil. How
time repeats itself.

Take a walk outside, and remember Dec the way it used to be, back in the
dark ages of computing. Be happy for what it was. It would want that. But
please, let it die with dignity.

Those of you who run Dec today is the equivalent of a dog's owner taking it
to a taxidermist after it has passed and still throwing it sticks.

VMS: Very Menstrual System

Here in Italy we love our culture, our history, the stuff that binds us
together. Sadly though, computing does not conjure up the same kind of
memories. It is there to be used and discarded after it has served its
purpose.

In closing, I would like to say that Dec was once great. However, it has
served its purpose and it is time to let it go.

Dec, you are dismissed.

